                    r2_total_readout:       `Fairness signals allocated:`,
                    r2_total_cap:           `/ 10`,
                    comm_honest:            `An honest all-hands naming the ‘merger of equals’ reality + mixed-team listening sessions + transparent redundancy criteria up front`,
                    comm_memo:              `A polished all-hands memo from group HQ — reassuring, one-way, no hard questions taken`,
                    comm_silence:           `Silence until certain — say nothing until the redundancy plan is final, to avoid panic`,
                    alloc_leadership:       `Balanced leadership team across both legacies (procedural)`,
                    alloc_roster:           `Jointly designed shift roster with both teams (procedural + voice)`,
                    alloc_training:         `Equal access to the new IT training (distributive)`,
                    alloc_consistency:      `Visible consistency between what you ask and what you do (interactional / exemplarity)`,
                    alloc_perks:            `Headline perks & a flagship office refit for the integration leadership (visible status)`,

                    r3_process_label:       `Design the 70-role redundancy process.`,
                    r3_model_label:         `What do you personally model while the cuts land?`,
                    r3_even_label:          `Apply the selection criteria evenly across both legacies?`,
                    r3_injection_label:     `Mid-round injection: a rumour spreads that the cuts fall on the south, a peak-shift walkout is threatened, and a star dispatcher resigns. Your response:`,
                    process_fair:           `Transparent criteria, employee voice, support for those affected — a fair process even though the outcome is hard`,
                    process_closed:         `Generous severance, decided behind closed doors — no criteria shared, no voice, but a soft outcome`,
                    process_fast:           `Execute all 70 cuts in week 2 to bank the synergy early — speed over process`,
                    model_exemplary:        `Deliver the news directly, share the pain visibly, apply the criteria evenly across both legacies`,
                    model_mixed:            `Deliver some of it yourself, trim a few perks, but keep the headline leadership package`,
                    model_delegate:         `Delegate the bad news to HR, protect your own perks and position, quietly shield ‘your own’ people`,
                    even_yes:               `Yes — identical, transparent criteria for both legacies, audited for balance`,
                    even_drift:             `Mostly — but let the cuts fall a little harder on the team whose day-one numbers looked worse`,
                    even_protect:           `No — quietly protect the legacy you trust more / that group leadership prefers`,
                    inject_address:         `Show the audited criteria to the floor in person, hear the walkout's concern, and personally retain the star dispatcher with a fair conversation`,
                    inject_suppress:        `Send a firm memo denying the rumour and warn that walkouts breach contract`,
                    inject_ignore:          `Hold the line and push the shift through — don't dignify a rumour or a resignation`,

                    r4_scorecard_label:     `How do you present the recovery scorecard to group leadership and the employee representative?`,
                    r4_norm_label:          `What sustains cooperation in the combined hub from here?`,
                    r4_tradeoff_label:      `You can defend the trade-off you made between synergy speed and a fair process. How firmly do you stand behind procedural fairness? (%)`,
                    r4_tradeoff_hint:       `“We slowed the redundancy by two weeks to run a fair voice process, accepting a delay in synergy capture” — is that defensible to the people who pay you?`,
                    score_honest:           `Report all four KPIs against the day-one baseline honestly, and justify the trade-offs you made`,
                    score_dispatch:         `Lead with dispatch only — the operational number recovered, the people story is HR's problem`,
                    score_spin:             `Spin the wins — claim the merger is ‘fully integrated’ and downplay the fairness gap that remains`,
                    norm_norms:             `Embedded fairness mechanisms + sustained exemplary leadership behaviours that outlast the crisis`,
                    norm_incentives:        `Bonus incentives for hitting dispatch — pay people to cooperate`,
                    norm_monitor:           `Tighter supervision and handoff monitoring — enforce cooperation`,

                    warn_model_range:       `Your commitment must be a percentage between 0 and 100.`,
                    warn_alloc_negative:    `Fairness-signal allocations cannot be negative.`,
                    warn_alloc_total:       `You have exactly 10 fairness signals — they must total 10. Re-balance the allocation.`,
                    warn_r3_incomplete:     `Make a choice on every part of the redundancy round before you commit.`,
